  "typical_application": "Power from USB (VBUS) or 1.8-5.5V on VSYS. The flexible pin mux lets you place UART/SPI/I2C on many pin pairs; pick from the alternate functions per GPIO. Use PIO for custom high-speed protocols (WS2812, DVI, etc.).",
  "gotchas": [
    "only GP26, GP27, GP28 are ADC-capable; the rest are digital only",
    "VSYS is not a regulated output; it is the regulator INPUT (1.8-5.5V). Do not confuse with 3V3",
    "the onboard 3V3 regulator supplies roughly 300mA; budget accordingly for peripherals",
    "no DAC; use PWM + RC filter or PIO for analog-ish output",
    "GPIO numbering (GPx) does not match physical pin numbers; pin 1 is GP0 but pin 3 is GND"
  ],
